<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali ibn Ghaniya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1188">1188</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ali ibn Ishaq ibn Ghaniya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali ibn Ghaniya was a member of the Banu Ghaniya, the Almoravid family ruling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a>. In 1184 he landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a>, seized it from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> and began a long war to restore Almoravid rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>, recognising the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> and allying with Arab tribes and Qaraqush. He was killed in 1188, and his brother Yahya continued the struggle.</p></div>
